# Scacelith - Slovenščina
# Translation of assets/i18n/en.lang (same keys, same {n}). Plurals have four forms:
# one (1, 101...)|two (2, 102...)|few (3-4, 103-104...)|other (0, 5-100...).
# Register: formal "vi" (lower case mid-sentence), as Microsoft and Google Slovenian software: help
# texts and prompts in the formal imperative or a "vi" question ("Izberite", "Ali želite ..."); buttons,
# menu entries and commands in the short command form, a 2nd person singular imperative or a noun
# ("Shrani", "Prekliči", "Ponudi remi", "Nova partija"); sentence case. Titles are in capitals (the
# title face is an inscriptional capital face).
# The player's gender is unknown: the polite past tense ("ste ponudili") is the standard plural form
# for any reader, but nouns, the present tense or impersonal phrasing are preferred ("Zmaga", "Vaš
# poraz", "Odjava je uspela"); no adjective or passive participle agreeing with the player.
# Chess terms of the Slovenian chess federation (ŠZS): kralj, dama, trdnjava, lovec, skakač, kmet;
# poteza (f), zapisnik (scoresheet), tempo igre (time control), rating, remi, sodnik (arbiter),
# polpoteza (ply). White / Black as players: "beli" / "črni" (masculine).
# Quality levels are feminine (they agree with "kakovost"); gif.wait.* are accusative (they only
# follow "čez"). engine.million uses the abbreviation "mio." (no agreement with the number).
# Keep the sections: other parts of the game add their keys in sections of their own.

